{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792310607,"nonce":"oiFCpuCUSeZmblL0Ckjh6O6iskg=","title":"VERIFIED LEAK in plain Haxe: a heap object stored into another object's field is never freed. The wrapper IS freed; its contents are not. ...","message":"**VERIFIED 2026-08-20 at 9b1ebd5c.** Runnable repro committed:\n`scripts/check_composition_leak.sh` — **it exits 1 today**; it reports an OPEN bug,\nit is not a passing guard.\n\n```\n  no wrapper (control)      32,752,216      32,604,736     FLAT\n  object held in a field    98,058,888     161,694,368     LINEAR\n```\n\n\n`new Box(c)` where `Box` stores `c` in a field: **`Box` IS freed, `c` is NOT.**\n`insert_free` reads the constructor's store of its parameter into a field as an\nescape (`param_retained`, insert_free.rs ~:1966), so the argument stops being freed\nat the caller — and nothing frees it when the wrapper dies.\n\n**NO ANNOTATIONS INVOLVED.** Plain Haxe. Nothing to do with `@:move`/`@:borrow`/\nMoveFlow — I checked all three by elimination.\n\n\nSHAPE-SENSITIVE. Scalar replacement normally erases the wrapper, and the store with\nit. **SRA declines the moment the wrapper POINTER is an argument to a call the\ninliner refused.** So a repro needs BOTH:\n1. a wrapper that outlives its constructor, AND\n2. a callee big enough not to inline (4 `if` branches was enough).\n\nA 3-branch kernel does NOT leak. That is why my first four attempts came back flat\nand I nearly reported \"cannot reproduce\".\n\n\n| shape | result |\n| --- | --- |\n| no wrapper, 4-branch kernel | FLAT |\n| wrapper holding an **Int** | FLAT |\n| wrapper holding a **heap object** | **LINEAR** |\n| `@:move` on owner only / on wrapper only / on both / on neither | ALL leak identically |\n\nA wrapper holding an Int does not leak ⇒ it is the FIELD STORE, not the wrapper\nallocation. `@:move` makes no difference in any combination ⇒ not an ownership bug.\n\n\nPREREQ = a sound `compute_param_retention` — same prerequisite as\n[[bugs_loop_body_class_alloc_never_freed]]. Do NOT patch `param_retained` blind:\n[[reference_insert_free_actual_conditions]] first, and note that\n[[bugs_release_guard_blind_to_call_shaped_frees]] and\n[[bugs_string_concat_in_loop_double_free]] are both past double-frees from this file.\nTool: `RAYZOR_DUMP_FREE_GRAPH` + free_graph_viewer.html. `RAYZOR_DUMP_MIR` is\nUSELESS here — it is PRE-optimisation, so `insert_free`'s output is not in it.\n\n\nmacOS: read **PEAK MEMORY FOOTPRINT** from `time -l`, never max RSS\n([[reference_macos_peak_footprint_is_the_metric]]). Run BOTH sizes — a single size\ntells you nothing, since the absolute number is dominated by the runtime. The\nsignal is growth vs the control's growth.\n\nFound by an adversarial workflow attacking a RefMut design; it surfaced as\n\"acquiring a handle leaks the owner\", and only stripping the annotations one at a\ntime showed it had nothing to do with handles or ownership at all.\n\n---\nArchived from Claude memory `bugs_field_store_object_never_freed` on 2026-10-18. A record of past work; open items in it may have their own issues.","files":null}]}